==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|provenance||origin}}, from {{uder|en|frm|provenant|}}, present participle of {{m|frm|provenir||come forth, arise}}, from {{uder|en|la|provenio||to come forth}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpɹɒ.və.nəns/|/ˈpɹɒ.və.ˌnɒns/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-provenance.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpɹɑ.və.nəns/|/ˈpɹoʊ.və.nɑns/|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|~}}

# Place or source of origin.
#: {{ux|en|Many supermarkets display the '''provenance''' of their food products.}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=2015|author=James Lambert|editors=Lan Li; Jamie McKeown; Liming Liu|chapter=Lexicography as a teaching tool: A Hong Kong case study|title=Dictionaries and corpora: Innovations in reference science. Proceedings of ASIALEX 2015 Hong Kong|publisher=The Hong Kong Polytechnic University|location=Hong Kong|page=147|passage=Within this melee of intersections between English and Cantonese, the students, being themselves bilingually fluent, were able to navigate with perfect ease in communicative contexts where the '''provenance''' of a certain term or expression matters little.}}
# {{lb|en|archaeology}} The place and time of origin of some [[artifact]] or other object. See '''Usage notes''' below.
#: {{ux|en|This spear is of Viking '''provenance'''.}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1982
|author=Thomas Lawton
|chapter=Bronze Vessels, Fittings, and Weapons
|title=Chinese Art of the Warring States Period
|url=https://archive.org/details/chineseartofwarr00lawt/
|publisher=w:Smithsonian Institution
|ISBN=0-934686-50-5
|LCCN=82-600184
|OCLC=13520365
|OL=8390737M
|page=79
|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/chineseartofwarr00lawt/page/79/
|column=1
|text=Further support for the Shansi '''provenance''' came in 1965, when a bronze quadruped with identical ornamentation and of approximately the same size as the Freer example was unearthed in tomb 126, at Fen-shui-ling, Ch'ang-chih, Shansi Province.}}
# {{lb|en|arts}} The history of ownership of a work of art.
#: {{ux|en|The picture is of royal '''provenance'''.}}
# {{lb|en|computing}} The copy history of a piece of data, or the intermediate pieces of data used to compute a final data element, as in a database record or web site (data provenance).
# {{lb|en|computing}} The execution history of computer processes which were used to compute a final piece of data (process provenance).
# {{lb|en|of a person}} Background; history; place of origin.
#: {{syn|en|ancestry}}

====Usage notes====
* The term [[provenience]] in archaeology has largely replaced ''provenance'' because ''provenience'' is restricted to [[in situ]] location at the date of archaeological discovery rather than the "origin-to-present" [[chain of custody]] details of proper ''provenance'' as is customarily used by historians, museums, and commercial entities.

